WEBVTT

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.420
I overlay three Level 2 Giant Germs!

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:14.350
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:15.700
Xyz Summon!

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.230
A Number is coming!

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.660
Appear, Number 96!

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.340
Dark Mist!

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.170
100 ATK?

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.950
Isn’t it weak?

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.010
You can’t defeat me with that Number!

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:39.640
Wait, Yuma!

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.520
Watch what the opponent does first!

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.690
Don’t attack carelessly!

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.650
Utopia attacks Dark Mist!

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.110
Yuma!

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.530
Go, Utopia!

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.200
Hope Sword Slash!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.500
I did it! What a great victory!

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.220
Incredible, Yuma!

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.480
Yeah! It was a perfect victory!

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.630
Did you see that?

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.860
There isn’t a Number that can defeat me!

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.230
Just because you won...

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:41.870
But Utopia’s attack was a bit forced.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:44.580
It’s fine. That Number wasn’t special—

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.010
You didn’t know that!

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.640
You don’t know what monsters your opponent has!

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.450
But I won!

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.890
It’s my way of doing things!

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.590
How dare you talk like that?

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.600
Shut up!

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.030
Stop it!

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.250
Who should I duel today?

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.910
They might be serious this time.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.630
The destruction of the world...

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:45.140
That’s also my memory.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.370
It’s been three days.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:52.980
Tetsuo and I have never gone
this long without dueling.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.190
I’m Yuma Tsukumo!

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.120
My dream is to become duel champion!

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.410
Hey, you!

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.130
Are you good at dueling?

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.500
I’ve never won yet.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.970
You fool!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.590
Then he challenges me.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.220
How dare you laugh at me?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.310
If you’re upset, then beat me!

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.550
Duel!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.320
I totally lost.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.620
But Tetsuo still let me
duel him repeatedly.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:37.060
Even though he kept losing,
he challenged me everyday.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.610
I’ll never give up!

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:46.470
After watching him duel, I...

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.720
Apologize?

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.490
Because one of you has to apologize.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.690
But it’s his fault!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.960
Yuma, are you really fine
with how things are?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.320
Don’t friends talk everyday
to understand each other’s hearts?

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.270
Friends?

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.570
I’m not friends with him!

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:30.370
Tetsuo!

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.260
It’s your fault for suddenly grabbing me!

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.140
What’s this?

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:00.270
Astral!

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.680
What?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.910
You’re Number 96!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.370
What are you talking about?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:23.130
I was waiting for this moment when I could possess you and become whole!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:27.890
I’ll destroy everything!

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.350
What?

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:37.850
What’s this?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.020
Yuma!

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.080
Let me go!

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.030
It’s pointless.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.060
You can no longer escape.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.990
Yuma, give Utopia to Tetsuo.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.450
Utopia?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.740
Give it to him!

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.130
Tetsuo!

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.800
Utopia?

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.260
Astral!

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:13.970
Now I’ve become the most powerful Number!

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.690
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:23.820
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.610
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.990
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:38.380
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:44.820
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:51.470
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:55.350
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:58.480
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.270
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.650
Everyone is not the same

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.570
That’s the reason for living

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:13.820
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:19.250
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.500
I travel to the edge of the world

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.960
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.020
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.050
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.430
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:40.100
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:49.940
\hThe Dark Number: Dark Yuma vs Tetsuo\h

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:49.940
Number 20:

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.690
How dare you hurt Astral?

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.940
Hey, kid!

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:53.280
Hand over the Number!

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.370
Tetsuo, what just happened?

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:07.310
I don’t know, but it might be this key’s power.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.090
You...

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:17.680
If I defeat him and give Yuma the King’s Key,
I might be able to save Yuma!

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.810
If you want the Number so badly,
then beat me in a duel!

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.350
A duel?

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.490
Don’t do it, Tetsuo!

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:27.790
He’s very dangerous!
Hurry up and run!

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.020
I can’t leave you!

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:31.090
But...

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:33.330
If you were in my position,
would you run away?

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.630
Would you leave me and run?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:36.490
Tetsuo...

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:39.080
Interesting.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.830
I’ll face you!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.640
Duel Disk set!

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.820
D-Gazer set!

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:50.850
AR Vision Link complete.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.800
Duel!

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:56.920
You have no freedom.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:58.350
You are my minion.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:03.730
Even though Astral is my opponent,
I’ve memorized Yuma’s deck completely.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:05.770
I go first!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.700
My turn! I draw!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:11.150
I summon Aye-Iron!

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:20.080
I equip the Equip Spell
Spring Punch on to Aye-Iron!

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.710
Aye-Iron’s effect activates!

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:29.290
Once per turn, it gains 400 ATK.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.250
Now Spring Punch’s effect activates!

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:39.890
When the equipped monster’s ATK increase, you take half its ATK as damage! That’s 1000 points!

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.850
Yuma!

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.070
I’m fine.

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.840
Keep it coming!

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.700
I activate the Continuous Spell Gearspring Catapult and end my turn!

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:00.870
Just wait, Yuma! I’ll save you!

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:04.720
My turn. I draw!

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:06.830
I Special Summon Acorno!

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:12.800
I can Special Summon this card by sending one card in my hand to the graveyard.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:18.300
And when I send Pinecono from my hand to the graveyard, I can Special Summon it.

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:21.310
Resurrect, Pinecono!

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.930
Then I summon Darklon!

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:34.690
When Darklon is successfully summoned, all monsters on my field change to DARK Attribute and gain 1 Level.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:40.360
I overlay Level 2 Acorno, Pinecono and Darklon!

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:44.620
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.950
Xyz Summon!

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:53.210
Appear, my copy Number 96!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.580
The envoy from the dark! Dark Mist!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.940
This is Dark Mist?

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.810
It’s completely different from before!

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:09.480
This is Dark Mist’s true appearance.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.610
Dark Mist attacks Aye-Iron!

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:15.270
Attack with 100 ATK?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.430
I activate Dark Mist’s effect.

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:28.470
By using one Overlay Unit, your monster’s ATK are halved, and Dark Mist gains the lost ATK!

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.280
Shadow Gain!

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:38.810
That means it will always have more ATK than the opponent!

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:42.800
Exactly. Go, Dark Mist!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.970
Black Mirage Whip!

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.980
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:56.210
This is Dark Mist’s power...

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:58.690
My turn! I draw!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:02.700
I activate the Continuous Spell Gearspring Catapult’s effect!

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:06.910
Every time it’s my turn, it gains one Windup Counter.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.580
Counter?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:12.670
It needs to use counters to activate its effect.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:17.130
You’re planning to amass counters to power up your spell card’s effect.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.700
I summon Tin Goldfish!

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.840
I activate Iron Call from my hand!

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:33.140
When there’s a Machine-Type monster on the field, I can Special
Summon a Level 4-or-below Machine-Type monster from the graveyard.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.750
Resurrect, Aye-Iron!

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:41.820
I activate the spell card Iron Draw from my hand!

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:47.570
When there are two Machine-Type monsters on the field, I draw two cards from my deck!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.130
Yuma, I promise to save you.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:56.540
I overlay Level 4 Tin Goldfish and Aye-Iron!

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:00.360
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:02.160
Xyz Summon!

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:07.590
Appear, Number 39: Utopia!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.040
Utopia...

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:19.190
You appeared, Number 39.

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:23.570
What’s this?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.170
This is the Number’s power...

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:34.120
Yuma! I activate Gearspring Catapult’s effect!

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:40.700
I use one Windup Counter to increase Utopia’s ATK by 500 this turn.

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.440
3000 ATK!

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:43.460
All right!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.130
Go, Utopia!

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:49.680
You don’t know how terrifying Dark Mist is.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.970
Dark Mist’s effect activates!

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.420
Shadow Gain!

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.690
What?

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:01.690
You can activate Shadow Gain’s effect even when you don’t attack?

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.650
It took Utopia’s ATK!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.070
Go, Dark Mist!

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:10.280
Tetsuo!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.370
Black Mirage Whip!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:15.170
I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:18.170
One monster’s attack is negated!

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.170
Moon Barrier!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.790
All right, you did it!

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.930
It’s just as I planned.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.220
I activate the trap Counterforce!

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:39.400
When a battle is negated, you take damage equal to the difference in the battling monsters’ ATK.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:43.570
Tetsuo takes 1100 points of damage?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.300
Tetsuo!

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:55.790
Now do you understand that you can’t defeat me?

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:00.520
Tetsuo...

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:10.380
That incredible monster can gain ATK when it attacks or is attacked.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.230
I’m sorry, Tetsuo.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:14.560
Yuma...

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.670
Yuma...

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.640
Astral, is that you?

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:23.730
Yuma, listen to me carefully.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:28.650
I activate the Continuous Spell Automatic Gearspring Machine from my hand!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:32.180
When this card activates,
it has two Windup Counters.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:36.520
Every time it’s my turn again,
it gains one counter.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:42.920
If I send this card to the graveyard,
I can move its Windup Counters to a different card!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.840
You’re planning to amass even more counters.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.880
I set one card and end my turn!

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:54.850
Gearspring Catapult’s effect ends,
so Utopia loses 500 ATK.

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:00.680
What?

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:01.850
Yuma!

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:11.790
I’ve finally taken him over.

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:13.660
My turn! I draw!

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:17.620
Dark Mist attacks Utopia!

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:20.390
And I activate its effect.

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:21.580
Shadow Gain!

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:30.300
I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.470
Moon Barrier!

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:34.800
You think that will protect you?

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.140
I activate the trap Overlay Banish!

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:43.230
Your monster’s effect
that requires an Overlay Unit is negated!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:47.610
Go, Black Mirage Whip!

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.820
Tetsuo!

00:16:58.110 --> 00:17:01.950
Next, I’ll destroy Gearspring Catapult.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.620
What?

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:12.550
I knew that you would amass counters on Gearspring Catapult so that you could power up the next monster you summon!

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.490
You’re wrong.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:20.620
He’s planning to finish you with a single strike.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:22.060
Single strike?

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:25.660
His set card is Gearspring Exploder.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.520
Don’t tell him, Yuma!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:31.020
It’s no use. He can’t hear you.

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:40.680
When it’s his turn and he gains counters, Gearspring Exploder deals 800 points of damage for every counter on his field.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:41.940
800 points?

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:49.710
On his next turn, Gearspring Catapult and Automatic Gearspring Machine will each gain one counter for a total of four counters.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:53.690
In other words, it will deal 3200 points of damage.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:57.060
If that card activates, we lose.

00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:59.010
I see.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:00.970
Yuma!

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:05.000
In that case, I’ll destroy that set card!

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:08.940
I activate the Quick-Play Spell
Xyz Cyclone from my hand!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:16.740
When an Xyz Monster is destroyed,
one trap card is destroyed!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.910
Gearspring Exploder was destroyed...

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.850
I end my turn.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:25.860
Well done, Yuma. Now I’ll win.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.470
Yuma...

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:33.590
I’ll never give up!

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.300
Damn!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:39.880
If I was Yuma, I’d never give up!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:43.600
Gearspring Catapult?

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:45.580
Yuma...

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:50.440
My turn! I draw!

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.150
It’s here!

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:58.960
Due to their effects, I put one counter each on Gearspring Catapult and Automatic Gearspring Machine!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.580
It’s pointless to keep fighting.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:12.980
I remove three counters from Automatic Gearspring Machine to Special Summon Gearspring Spirit from my hand!

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:22.470
Once per turn, Gearspring Spirit lowers one of your monsters’ ATK to 0 until the End Phase!

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:23.640
What?

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:31.820
I activate the spell card Monster Reborn from my hand!

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:34.560
Come, Utopia!

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.480
Utopia resurrected!

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:38.870
What’s happening?

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:45.450
You did it, Tetsuo!

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.010
What’s going on?

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:51.420
Yuma pretended to be taken over.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:58.340
If you destroyed Gearspring Catapult,
there’s no way I could win.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:04.300
That’s why Yuma pretended to be taken over so that he could protect Gearspring Catapult.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.760
What a cheap trick!

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:10.230
Our power of friendship won’t lose against you!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:13.690
I activate Gearspring Catapult’s effect!

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:20.140
By removing one Windup Counter,
Utopia gains 500 ATK!

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.450
3000 ATK!

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:28.410
You can’t use Dark Mist’s effect anymore!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.410
You lose, Number 96!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.170
Go, Tetsuo!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.130
This is my kattobing!

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:46.340
No way!

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.510
Hope Sword Slash!

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:01.490
Impossible! I...

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.450
Yuma, catch!

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:25.330
You did it, Tetsuo!

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:26.640
Yuma!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:32.680
I’m impressed that you came up
with a comeback combo.

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:36.310
I guess...

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.880
Was it Astral’s idea?

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:45.020
No... But he gave me a little advice.

00:21:45.020 --> 00:21:46.250
I knew it.

00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:49.490
Because it was too good of an idea.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:52.990
It’s because you wouldn’t defeat him quickly!

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:56.130
How dare you say that when I saved you?

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:58.330
Yuma, Tetsuo...

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.640
You saved me.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:04.010
Number 96...

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:07.050
This Number is...

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:15.350
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:17.350
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:22.790
How many monsters do you need to tribute to summon a Level 10 monster?

00:22:22.790 --> 00:22:24.820
1 or 2?

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:34.970
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.970 --> 00:22:39.880
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:54.560
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:59.480
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:01.900
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:04.770
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:06.900
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:08.820
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.710
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:18.040
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.590 --> 00:23:23.650
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.650 --> 00:23:28.090
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:33.220
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:37.240
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.580 --> 00:23:44.340
We rescued the city’s cleaning robot.

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:45.150
Its name is Obomi.

00:23:45.580 --> 00:23:47.710
It’s our newest friend!

00:23:47.710 --> 00:23:51.650
But someone is using Obomi to steal jewelry.

00:23:51.650 --> 00:23:55.450
What’s going on? Why are you doing that?

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:59.120
Yuma, Obomi no longer remembers you.

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:03.500
In that case, I’ll duel you and return you to normal!

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:09.880
\h\hYuma vs Cleaning Robot Obomi\h\h

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:07.770
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Yuma vs Cleaning Robot Obomi”

00:24:07.770 --> 00:24:09.880
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.810 --> 00:24:13.410
The answer is...

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:14.670
2!

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:19.150
You can summon it by tributing
two monsters on the field.

00:24:19.550 --> 00:24:24.030
This is called a Tribute Summon.
